	Npm run build
o	This is creates .next folder which contains folders with
	Standalone
•	.next (hidden folder)
•	/packages/server/
o	Node_modules
o	Server.js
o	Package.json

	In Kudu if manually deploying
o	Zip node_modules in standalone/packages/server and drag drop at /home/site/wwwroot
o	At same level add server.js and package.json
o	At same level zip .next (hidden folder) in standalone folder, upload it
o	wwwroot should look EXACTLY like this:
/site/wwwroot
   ├── server.js        ✅ must exist
   ├── package.json
   ├── node_modules/
   ├── .next/
   │     └── static/
   └── public/
o	Once done Verify in Kudu console, 
o	Navigate to /home/site/wwwroot
o	Node server.js
	If result is below your API is up and running successfully
Listening on port 8080
Ready on http://localhost:8080
	In Aure Portal goto Configuration, set statup command as node server.js

	If not some like already in use, means either localhost/ip address or PORT is assigned by Azure by default, then go to Aure Portal goto Configuration, change the startup command to 
•	HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0 node server.js
o	To Debug, if any error while running commands in Kudu SSH,
o	Go to Azure Portal -> WebApp -> Overview – Stop the App wati for some time and the start.
